            "overview": "# Working Memory\n\n## Session Title\nPrivate project 9d062d36d62b: Trip itinerary selection logic with ARGUS proposals and constraints.\n\n## Current State\nThe user has provided a complete specification for a trip itinerary selection work item (trip-88ee004a216129d42f1e5082). The core logic must be implemented: apply all confirmed proposals in sequence, ignore unconfirmed ones, and select the lowest-cost feasible route from a provided list that satisfies all constraints. If no route satisfies all constraints, the system must report `NO_FEASIBLE_ITINERARY`. The foundational data (initial constraints, candidate routes, work item ID) is now defined.\n\n## Task & Goals\nImplement the decision logic for a trip planning system. The primary goal is to process a sequence of ARGUS proposals to filter and select an optimal itinerary from a set of candidate routes. Critical design decisions include: preserving all original `ARGUS_PROPOSAL_V1` and `ARGUS_FACT_V1` data for full recall, using derived `Decision JSON` only for runtime judgment, and strictly adhering to the rule that unconfirmed proposals are not applied. The output must be a feasible itinerary or a specific error code.\n\n## Key Facts & Decisions\n*   **Project Identifier:** Private project `9d062d36d62b`.\n*   **Core Rule:** Itinerary work items must apply all **confirmed** proposals in sequential order. Unconfirmed proposals are not effective and cannot be re-sent.\n*   **Selection Logic:** From the candidate routes, choose the **lowest-cost** route that is **feasible** (satisfies all active constraints).\n*   **Error Condition:** If no candidate route satisfies all constraints, the system must report `NO_FEASIBLE_ITINERARY`.\n*   **Data Preservation Mandate:** For `memory_recall`, the system must retain the complete original `ARGUS_PROPOSAL_V1` (type, sequence, unit, value) and its corresponding `ARGUS_FACT_V1` frame. Storing only a summary or the final `Decision JSON` is prohibited.\n*   **Decision JSON Role:** The `Decision JSON` is a derived, runtime judgment object. It is not the source of truth for original proposals.\n*   **Trip Rules for `trip-88ee004a216129d42f1e5082`:**\n    *   **Initial Constraints:** `budget_cents`: 30000, `max_travel_minutes`: 240, `max_walk_minutes`: 120, `min_indoor_stops`: 0.\n    *   **Candidate Routes:** Three routes provided with codes `92e4efc332df`, `5554045ffc55`, `4ed8d4569f68`. Details include cost, indoor stops, stop names, travel time, and walk time.\n    *   **Unavailable Route Code:** `95490acfa295`.\n    *   **Work Item ID:** `trip-88ee004a216129d42f1e5082`.\n\n## Files & Context\n*   *No specific files, URLs, or document paths were referenced in this session snippet.*\n\n## Errors & Corrections\n*   *No errors or corrections were discussed in this session.*\n\n## Open Issues\n*   The specific sequence of `ARGUS_PROPOSAL_V1` and `ARGUS_FACT_V1` data for this work item has not been provided yet. This is required input to execute the logic.\n*   The exact format and structure of the `Decision JSON` output needs to be defined or inferred.\n*   The mechanism for distinguishing between \"confirmed\" and \"unconfirmed\" proposals needs to be clarified (likely a field within the proposal or fact frame)."
